diff --git a/findings.md b/findings.md
index 8a67766a..e41b3adc 100644
--- a/findings.md
+++ b/findings.md
@@ -324,3 +324,91 @@ knowledge pieces. Append in-the-moment; synthesise at project close.
   per-context behavior. The fragility tax is the upstream-rename
   risk — mitigated by a regression test that drives the synthetic
   call shape.
+
+---
+
+## ERP-LATENT-FIX — MOCK-SELECT predicate fix (2026-05-11)
+
+### Errors
+- **`set_table_data` with a dict-shape payload masks the missing-id
+  bug differently from the list-shape.** `set_table_data("clientes",
+  {"arquivado": False, "nome": "João"})` wraps the dict to `[dict]`
+  via `_data = copy.deepcopy([data])` in `MockRequestBuilder.__init__`
+  — so the SELECT predicate-filter DOES evaluate and DOES strip the
+  row when `.eq("id", "c1")` finds no matching `id` key. Initial
+  read of `_filtered_rows` ("non-list → return as-is") missed the
+  earlier __init__ list-wrap. Fix: read the init carefully + don't
+  assume `_filtered_rows`'s dict short-circuit fires.
+- **Defusedxml dep gap is NOT a MOCK-SELECT issue.** 940 collection
+  ERRORs + 24 xml_feeds FAILs all root-cause to `ModuleNotFoundError:
+  defusedxml` (in `requirements.txt` but not installed in the
+  runtime python3.11). Out of MOCK-SELECT scope; surfaced as
+  architect-followup at end-of-report.
+
+### Mistakes / slips
+- **First pass conflated "53 FAILED" with "53 latent-fix candidates".**
+  Initial scan suggested all 53 failed tests were predicate-filter
+  victims. Closer look: 24 were defusedxml-blocked (xml_feeds_service
+  tests). Actual MOCK-SELECT scope was 29 tests across 13 files —
+  ~55% of the apparent count. Lesson: classify by ROOT CAUSE before
+  scoping, not by failure-LIST length.
+
+### Lessons
+- **The PF reference fix shape applies cleanly to ERP, but the
+  tenancy columns differ.** PF's predicate filter is uniformly
+  `eq("org_id", self.org_id)` — single-key fix. ERP services use
+  more varied filters: `corretor_id` (agenda), `extrato_id`+`conciliado`
+  (banco), `id` (clientes), `status`+`data_vencimento` (contratos /
+  seguros / impostos), `tipo`+`status`+`org_id` (certidoes TJSP),
+  `campanha_id` (marketing), `usuario_id` (metas existing-check),
+  `status` (recorrencia), `arquivado` (relatorios funnel). One-key
+  vs many-key product-specific tenancy: scan the production SELECT
+  for ALL `.eq()`/`.neq()`/`.lt()`/`.gte()` calls along the chain
+  and add EVERY column that gates row inclusion.
+- **Tests asserting "mock returns 2 rows for both queries so 4
+  total" rely on ignore-filter quirk.** `test_overdue_records_counted`
+  expected `count==4` because the unfiltered mock returned the same
+  2 rows for BOTH the pendente AND parcial SELECTs. Under predicate
+  filtering each query matches only the rows with its own status —
+  need to seed 2+2 distinct rows. Fix shape: read the test's
+  assertion → if it counts queries × shared-rows, redistribute rows
+  across the queries.
+
+### Interesting findings
+- **`gte("created_at", cutoff)` requires the seed row to have a
+  `created_at` newer than cutoff — use NOW, not a fixed past date.**
+  `marketing_service.process_alerts` filters ativos by `gte
+  (created_at, now - 7d)`. Pinning to a fixed ISO date risks the
+  cutoff drifting past the seed date over time. Better: compute
+  `_NOW_ISO = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()` once at module
+  load.
+- **`_delayed_tjsp_process` has a finally block that calls
+  `schedule_tjsp_for_org` regardless of the early-return path** —
+  so `test_skips_item_no_longer_queued` and
+  `test_chains_next_item_after_completion` pass by accident under
+  predicate filtering (the early-return strips the seeded row, but
+  the finally still fires the mock). Only the assertion on
+  `_process_single_tjsp_item.assert_called_once()` actually breaks.
+  Test-of-the-finally is more robust than test-of-the-mainline here.
+
+### Knowledge pieces
+- **MOCK-SELECT latent-fix shape, ERP-specific:**
+  1. Run pytest; group failures by file.
+  2. For each failing test, open the production code and grep all
+     `.eq()`/`.neq()`/`.in_()`/`.lt()`/`.gt()`/`.gte()`/`.lte()`
+     calls along the SELECT chain.
+  3. Add EVERY filtered column to the seed row. Use sentinel values
+     that satisfy the predicate (past date for `.lt(today)`, "ativo"
+     for `eq("status", "ativo")`, matching id for `.eq("id", X)`).
+  4. For tests asserting cross-query row reuse, redistribute rows
+     across the now-filtered queries.
+  5. Forward-compatibility: extra columns on a seed row never break
+     the pre-fix "ignore filter" semantics. Safe to ship even before
+     MOCK-SELECT-PREDICATE-FIX is merged.
+- **defusedxml import-time blocker presents as 940 collection errors
+  in pytest** because `app.services.xml_feeds` is imported via
+  `app.services.__init__.py` → cascades through every router test
+  that touches `app.main`. Pre-existing dep gap (the package IS in
+  `requirements.txt`); separate from any MOCK-SELECT work. Diagnostic
+  pattern: `pytest --tb=line ... | grep ModuleNotFoundError | sort
+  -u` → if ALL errors share one root, it's a dep gap, not a test bug.
